r-invisible elementor-widget elementor-widget-text-editor\" data-id=\"d7be980\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-settings=\"{&quot;_animation&quot;:&quot;fadeInUp&quot;,&quot;_animation_delay&quot;:200}\" data-widget_type=\"text-editor.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<p>Need something cleared up? Here are our most frequently asked questions.<\/p>\t\t\t\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-66c0909 elementor-widget__width-initial elementor-widget elementor-widget-jkit_accordion\" data-id=\"66c0909\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"jkit_accordion.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div  class=\"jeg-elementor-kit jkit-accordion style-default jeg_module__4_69ff26a006d04\" ><div class=\"card-wrapper \">\n                <div class=\"card-header\">\n                    <a href=\"#expand-d49999f\" class=\"card-header-button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" data-target=\"#expand-d49999f\" aria-controls=\"expand-d49999f\">\n                        <div class=\"left-icon-group\">\n                <div class=\"normal-icon\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"jki jki-plus-light\"><\/i><\/div>\n                <div class=\"active-icon\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"jki jki-minus-light\"><\/i><\/div>\n            <\/div><span class=\"title\">What is the shoulder stabilization surgery success rate?<\/span>\n                    <\/a>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"card-expand\" id=\"expand-d49999f\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"card-body\"><p>Shoulder stabilization surgery success rate depends on technique and patient factors. Arthroscopic Bankart repair for primary instability with minimal bone loss: 90-95% success preventing future dislocations. Bankart repair with Remplissage for Hill-Sachs defects: 85-90%. Latarjet procedure for significant glenoid bone loss (&gt;20-25%): 90-95% even in difficult cases. Capsular shift for multidirectional instability: 70-85%. Revision surgery after failed prior repair: 75-85%. Dr. Usama's fellowship training and experience consistently achieve outcomes at the higher end of these published success ranges. Factors improving success: good bone stock, proper surgical technique, patient compliance with rehabilitation, no premature return to sport<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n            <\/div><div class=\"card-wrapper \">\n                <div class=\"card-header\">\n                    <a href=\"#expand-339abdc\" class=\"card-header-button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" data-target=\"#expand-339abdc\" aria-controls=\"expand-339abdc\">\n                        <div class=\"left-icon-group\">\n                <div class=\"normal-icon\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"jki jki-plus-light\"><\/i><\/div>\n                <div class=\"active-icon\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"jki jki-minus-light\"><\/i><\/div>\n            <\/div><span class=\"title\">How long is shoulder stabilization surgery recovery?<\/span>\n                    <\/a>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"card-expand\" id=\"expand-339abdc\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"card-body\"><p>Shoulder stabilization recovery time follows a 4-phase protocol over 6-9 months for full return to contact sports. Sling for 4-6 weeks continuously. Desk work return: 1-2 weeks. Driving after shoulder stabilization: 6-8 weeks. Light manual labor: 3-4 months. Swimming and overhead activities: 4-5 months. Contact sports and full unrestricted activity: 6-9 months. Bankart surgery recovery time for complete strength return: 6-12 months depending on surgical complexity and your activity demands. How long is shoulder stabilization surgery itself? Procedure duration: 60-120 minutes depending on technique. Total time at surgical center: 3-4 hours including preparation and recovery before same-day discharge.<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n            <\/div><div class=\"card-wrapper \">\n                <div class=\"card-header\">\n                    <a href=\"#expand-cfd3e25\" class=\"card-header-button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" data-target=\"#expand-cfd3e25\" aria-controls=\"expand-cfd3e25\">\n                        <div class=\"left-icon-group\">\n                <div class=\"normal-icon\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"jki jki-plus-light\"><\/i><\/div>\n                <div class=\"active-icon\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"jki jki-minus-light\"><\/i><\/div>\n            <\/div><span class=\"title\">What is the difference between Bankart repair and Latarjet procedure?<\/span>\n                    <\/a>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"card-expand\" id=\"expand-cfd3e25\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"card-body\"><p>Bankart repair surgery reattaches the torn labrum (Bankart lesion) to the glenoid rim using suture anchors, this restores the soft tissue bumper preventing dislocation. Arthroscopic Bankart repair is the gold standard for primary instability with minimal bone loss (&lt;20%). Success rate: 90-95%. Latarjet procedure transfers bone from the coracoid process to the front of the glenoid socket, adding bony support where significant bone loss (&gt;20-25%) has occurred from repeated dislocations. The transferred bone acts as both a structural block and provides surface area for labral reattachment. Latarjet achieves 90-95% success even with significant bone loss where Bankart repair alone would fail. Dr. Usama determines which technique you need based on CT 3D reconstruction measuring exact bone loss percentage.<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n            <\/div><div class=\"card-wrapper \">\n                <div class=\"card-header\">\n                    <a href=\"#expand-751ef88\" class=\"card-header-button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" data-target=\"#expand-751ef88\" aria-controls=\"expand-751ef88\">\n                        <div class=\"left-icon-group\">\n                <div class=\"normal-icon\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"jki jki-plus-light\"><\/i><\/div>\n                <div class=\"active-icon\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"jki jki-minus-light\"><\/i><\/div>\n            <\/div><span class=\"title\">Can I return to contact sports after shoulder stabilization surgery?<\/span>\n                    <\/a>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"card-expand\" id=\"expand-751ef88\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"card-body\"><p>Yes. Return to sport after shoulder stabilization is achievable for 85-95% of athletes at pre-injury competition level. Timeline: non-contact sports (swimming, golf, tennis) 4-6 months; contact sports (rugby, football, martial arts, hockey) 6-9 months. Return clearance requires: 90%+ strength symmetry measured objectively vs opposite shoulder, full range of motion restoration, passing functional sport-specific tests, psychological readiness and confidence, and Dr. Usama's clinical clearance. Professional athletes across Dubai and UAE return to competition after shoulder dislocation surgery with proper rehabilitation. The key is patience, returning too early significantly increases re-dislocation risk. Physical therapy after bankart repair must be completed fully before sport clearance.<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n            <\/div><div class=\"card-wrapper \">\n                <div class=\"card-header\">\n                    <a href=\"#expand-fdae1f4\" class=\"card-header-button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" data-target=\"#expand-fdae1f4\" aria-controls=\"expand-fdae1f4\">\n                        <div class=\"left-icon-group\">\n                <div class=\"normal-icon\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"jki jki-plus-light\"><\/i><\/div>\n                <div class=\"active-icon\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"jki jki-minus-light\"><\/i><\/div>\n            <\/div><span class=\"title\">Is arthroscopic shoulder surgery for instability better than open surgery?<\/span>\n                    <\/a>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"card-expand\" id=\"expand-fdae1f4\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"card-body\"><p>Yes, for most cases. Arthroscopic shoulder stabilization delivers equal or superior outcomes to open surgery with significant advantages: same 90-95% success rates for primary repairs, less post-operative pain, same-day discharge (no hospital stay), faster return to activities, minimal scarring (3-4 tiny incisions vs 6-8 inch open incision), lower infection risk, and preserved muscle (no deltoid detachment needed). Open surgery still appropriate for: massive bone loss (Latarjet procedure traditionally open, though Dr. Usama performs arthroscopic-assisted), failed multiple prior arthroscopic repairs, severe capsular stretching requiring extensive plication. Dr. Usama performs 95%+ of shoulder dislocation surgery cases arthroscopically, reserving open surgery only for cases where arthroscopic technique is insufficient.<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n            <\/div><div class=\"card-wrapper \">\n                <div class=\"card-header\">\n                    <a href=\"#expand-78a45b0\" class=\"card-header-button\" aria-expanded=\"false\" data-target=\"#expand-78a45b0\" aria-controls=\"expand-78a45b0\">\n                        <div class=\"left-icon-group\">\n                <div class=\"normal-icon\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"jki jki-plus-light\"><\/i><\/div>\n                <div class=\"active-icon\"><i aria-hidden=\"true\" class=\"jki jki-minus-light\"><\/i><\/div>\n            <\/div><span class=\"title\">How much does shoulder stabilization surgery cost in Dubai?<\/span>\n                    <\/a>\n                <\/div>\n                <div class=\"card-expand\" id=\"expand-78a45b0\" style=\"display:none\"><div class=\"card-body\"><p>Shoulder stabilization surgery cost in Dubai varies based on surgical technique and facility. Arthroscopic Bankart repair: AED 35,000-55,000. Bankart with Remplissage: AED 40,000-60,000. Latarjet procedure: AED 50,000-70,000. Revision surgery: AED 45,000-65,000. These estimates include surgeon fees, facility fees, anesthesia, and initial post-operative visits. Most major UAE insurance plans cover medically necessary shoulder stabilization surgery Dubai procedures\u2014our team verifies your specific coverage and obtains pre-authorization before surgery so you know exactly what you'll pay. Bankart repair Dubai cost with insurance: typically AED 0-5,000 out-of-pocket depending on your plan.<\/p><\/div><\/div>\n            <\/div><\/div>\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-e7792d4 e-flex e-con-boxed wpr-particle-no wpr-jarallax-no wpr-parallax-no wpr-sticky-section-no wpr-column-slider-no wpr-equal-height-no e-con e-parent\" data-id=\"e7792d4\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<div class=\"e-con-inner\">\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-89d9290 e-con-full e-flex wpr-particle-no wpr-jarallax-no wpr-parallax-no wpr-sticky-section-no wpr-column-slider-no wpr-equal-height-no e-con e-child\" data-id=\"89d9290\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6d412d8 e-con-full e-flex wpr-particle-no wpr-jarallax-no wpr-parallax-no wpr-sticky-section-no wpr-column-slider-no wpr-equal-height-no e-con e-child\" data-id=\"6d412d8\" data-element_type=\"container\" data-e-type=\"container\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-element elementor-element-6b2ec89 elementor-widget elementor-widget-heading\" data-id=\"6b2ec89\" data-element_type=\"widget\" data-e-type=\"widget\" data-widget_type=\"heading.default\">\n\t\t\t\t<div class=\"elementor-widget-container\">\n\t\t\t\t\t<h2 class=\"elementor-heading-title elementor-size-default\">Related Conditions &amp; Procedures<\/h2>\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t\t\t<\/div>\n\t\t<div cl